    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Payments with a reference now go to that invoice instead of the earliest due one. Both acceptance tests pass with `bin/e2e`, and the earlier test-data replay that runs first also passed.\n\n**What changed:** the only real change is in `recordAutoPayment` in `InvoiceService.java`. This is the case where no invoice is open, no split is filled in and a reference is given. It now finds the selected client's invoice with that reference and applies the whole payment to it. It does this by recording a split payment with one part, so it reuses the checks that already exist: the amount can't be more than what's due, the invoice can't be a draft or void, and the date rules still apply.\n\n**When it's refused:**\n- **Mistyped reference:** caught by the existing checks, both in the form and on the server.\n- **Reference belongs to another client's invoice:** refused with \"\u2026 is not the reference of any of this client's invoices.\"\n- **Amount more than the invoice's amount due:** refused with the same message split payments already give.\n\nWithout a reference, payments still go to the earliest due invoices first, as before.\n\nThe front end already sent this case to the right endpoint and shows the server's error, so I only updated a comment there and one in `InvoiceController.java`.",
